{"container":null,"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"## Purpose\n\nA production gateway waits on several distinct things, and each wait fails differently. A connection timeout bounds TCP and TLS setup to an upstream. A first-byte timeout bounds how long the backend may compute before responding. An idle-stream timeout bounds silence between chunks once data is flowing. A total-request timeout caps the entire exchange so no client holds resources indefinitely.\n\n## Failure modes\n\nUsing one timeout for everything forces bad tradeoffs. A generous total limit lets a dead host consume sixty seconds of connect attempts. A tight one kills legitimate long downloads or server-sent event streams that are healthy but slow. Without an idle-stream limit, a backend that stalls mid-response leaves a partial body hanging. The client receives truncated data with no clear error, so the gateway must abort the stream visibly rather than pretend success. When any timeout fires, cancellation must propagate. The gateway should cancel the upstream request, signal downstream handlers, and stop retries tied to the expired deadline. Otherwise orphaned work keeps burning backend capacity. Connections abandoned mid-response must be closed rather than returned to the pool, because unread bytes would corrupt the next request that reuses that socket.\n\n## Operational guidance\n\nSet connect timeouts short and first-byte timeouts per route from observed latency percentiles. Tune idle timeouts to the expected streaming cadence, and derive total timeouts from the client's real deadline. Pass the remaining budget upstream through deadline headers. Emit distinct metrics for each timeout type so dashboards reveal whether failures stem from the network, slow computation, or stalled streams. Every phase of an upstream call needs its own deadline, and every expired deadline must cancel the work and discard the connection.","type":"text"}],"copilot_usage":{"token_details":[{"batch_size":1000000,"cost_per_batch":400000000000,"model":"claude-opus-5.5","token_count":150,"token_type":"input"},{"batch_size":1000000,"cost_per_batch":20000000000,"model":"claude-opus-5.5","token_count":0,"token_type":"cache_read"},{"batch_size":1000000,"cost_per_batch":500000000000,"model":"claude-opus-5.5","token_count":0,"token_type":"cache_write"},{"batch_size":1000000,"cost_per_batch":2000000000000,"model":"claude-opus-5.5","token_count":1557,"token_type":"output"}],"total_nano_aiu":3174000000},"id":"msg_011CfKuhWvw7oyfXyUg4wkCg","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"global","input_tokens":150,"output_tokens":1557,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":970}}}